Buttons
Add [btn] to a &lt;button&gt; or &lt;a&gt; for a primary accent button with --bevel and --raised shadows. Set btn-variant="secondary" for a bordered --color-surface button, or btn-variant="quiet" for a transparent button that highlights on hover. Set btn-variant="editable" for a full-width, dashed-border trigger with a text cursor for click-to-edit values. Change button size with btn-size="sm" or btn-size="lg", and add [btn-icon] for square icon-only buttons.
Setting aria-pressed="true" or aria-expanded="true" switches a button to --ui-held-face and --ui-held-shadow (--bevel-in and --sunken on primary and secondary buttons). Adding disabled lowers opacity to 50% and removes the shadow. The CSS never binds click handlers, toggles ARIA attributes, or turns a button into a link. Wrapper components default to type="button", whereas plain &lt;button btn&gt; elements follow native form defaults. On [btn][copy] and [btn][copyfor], setting [copied] swaps the first &lt;svg&gt;&lt;use&gt; icon for the second.
Setting aria-busy="true" hides child span and svg elements and shows a centred spinner immediately. With HTMX’s .htmx-request class, the same busy state appears after --busy-delay (default 200ms). Fast requests finish before the spinner appears. Under prefers-reduced-motion: reduce, button transitions are disabled and the spinner slows to 2s.

