Form controls, fields, and groups
Add [input], [textarea], or [select] for full-width sunken fields (--bevel-in and --sunken on --color-background); [input] also works on a container such as &lt;div input&gt; for mounted third-party inputs (for example, Stripe Elements). Browser spin buttons are hidden on [input][type="number"]. [textarea] starts at 5rem high, resizes vertically, and grows with its content via field-sizing: content. When a text, select, or choice control matches :user-invalid or [aria-invalid="true"], its border uses --hue-danger. Connect labels and hints with standard HTML for, id, and aria-describedby attributes.
Add [checkbox], [radio], [switch], or [range] to style native inputs while keeping native control behaviour. [checkbox] supports both :checked and :indeterminate states. Set --ui-range-fill (default 0%) on [range] to colour the filled track. Both [switch] and [range] reverse direction in right-to-left layouts. Under prefers-reduced-motion: reduce, control transitions are disabled. Under forced-colors: active, [checkbox], [radio], [switch], and [range] revert to appearance: auto.
Wrap a &lt;label&gt;, a [field-control] container, and an optional &lt;small&gt; hint in [field]. Adding any non-neutral [ui-tone] to &lt;small&gt; or &lt;p&gt; colours the text with --v2 both inside and outside [field]. Add [field-inline] to place a checkbox, radio, or switch beside its label with the hint underneath. A &lt;label&gt; inside [field] is dimmed when any descendant is :disabled. Use [fieldset] for a bordered &lt;fieldset&gt; and bold &lt;legend&gt;. Wrap adjacent [btn], [input], [textarea], or [select] elements in [group] to join them with shared borders and outer corner rounding. Focusing an input inside [group] draws one --ring outline around the group container. Add group-variant="inset" to place a compact [btn] inside a single bordered input box (use [cluster] for separate controls).

